# RoboCarl (AI brief)

Prefer this over codebase exploration. Open specific files only when editing them. **Update this rule** when levels, systems, or folder layout change.

## Game
2D URP portrait puzzle, playfield **9×19.5** (`AspectRatioCamera`). Player does **not** control Carl — Carl walks to closest **LOS-visible** oil/battery; player uses **draggable** or **button** walls. Energy drains ~25s; oil drains with walk. Energy 0 → lose. WinLine → MainMenu.

## Levels
| Level | Path | Notes |
|------:|------|-------|
| 1 | `LevelSession=1` → `SampleScene` | Scene: floors, ground Spring, WinLine, Carl. Spawns from `Resources/DefaultLevelSpawns` |
| 2 | `LevelSession=2` → **same** `SampleScene` | `Level2Layout.Apply()` strips Spring/WinLine/FloorRight; `Level2Spawns` (batteries, left `ButtonWall`, right `Spikes` + `DraggableWall`) |

- Menu levels 1–2 only (`MainMenuController`). Play Mode starts on `MainMenu`.
- **`Level2.unity` is unused** — not the L2 runtime path.
- `LevelSpawnConfig`: pickups, walls, buttonWalls, platforms, springs, spikes. Prefer editing those assets over `.unity` YAML.

## L1 anchors (SampleScene)
- Floor Y **-7.2** (thickness **0.08**, black). Carl start ~(0, -6.61).
- Ground spring ~(1, -7.335), size 1.2×0.35 — **top flush with floor top**.
- WinLine Y = `WinLine.DefaultHeight` (**-2.05**), full width.
- Spring tops must be walkable from the surface Carl is on (flush or within step-up ~20% of Carl height). Spawn position is the spring **center**, not the top.
- One-way platforms: thin lighter deck + corner supports; `PlatformEffector2D`; LOS ignores them so elevated pickups stay chaseable.
- Spikes: side hit → 25° knockback away (vx preserved; ground-brake disabled during knockback) + 1s grounded decision lock after settle; top hit → MainMenu. Not treated as ground; LOS ignores them.

## Scripts (`Assets/Scripts/`)
| Area | Files |
|------|-------|
| Carl | `CarlResources`, `CarlLocomotion`, `CarlPickupChaser`, `CarlVisual`, `CarlSparkEffect` |
| Level | `GameDirector` (spawn walls/button walls/platforms/springs/spikes), `LevelSession`, `Level2Layout`, `Data/LevelSpawnConfig` |
| Props | `ResourcePickup`, `SpringPad`, `OneWayPlatform`, `WinLine`, `DraggableWall`, `ButtonWall`, `Spikes` |
| UI / audio | `MainMenuController`, `MenuUi`, `LoseOverlay` (restart = active scene name), `GameMusic`, `GameSfx`, `GameAudioSettings` |
| Visual helpers | `GameSprites`, `SpriteQuad` — procedural props use `GameSprites.White` (never null material); `AspectRatioCamera` + `CarlCameraFollow` (vertical smooth chase, Carl ~1/3 up screen) |

## Conventions
- Input System **only** — no legacy `Input.*` for gameplay
- New interactables: build visual in code + Rules entry + `LevelSpawnConfig` if level-driven
- **Do not regenerate `.meta` GUIDs** — hand-assigned; breaks SO/scene refs
- Art: Carl PNGs via `Resources/CarlAppearance`; UI icons `Resources/UI/`. `*.png`/`*.wav` are normal Git blobs (not LFS)

## Layout
```
Assets/Art/         source PNGs
Assets/Resources/   Audio, UI, *Spawns, CarlAppearance
Assets/Scripts/     gameplay (+ Data/)
Assets/Scenes/      MainMenu, SampleScene (L1+L2 base), Level2 (unused)
Assets/Editor/      PlayModeStartScene
Assets/Settings/    URP
```
